The [[☃ definition 2]] will pass through points $(3,h(3))$ and $(7,h(7))$.

$\begin{align}
\text{slope}&=\dfrac{\text{change in }y}{\text{change in }x}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{h(7)-h(3)}{7-3}
\end{align}$

![Function h is graphed. The x-axis goes from negative 1 to 8. The graph consists of a curve. The curve starts in quadrant 2, moves downward with decreasing steepness through points (3, h of 3) and (7, h of 7), and ends in quadrant 1. A secant line connects the 2 points.](web+graphie:${☣ LOCALPATH}/images/a955ecd159ff92cfdd4a93e26aa24ce6afca5b24)

We will need to know the values of $h(3)$ and $h(7)$ to find the slope.

$\begin{align}
h(3)&=\sqrt{15-2(3)}
\\\\
&=3
\\\\
h(7)&=\sqrt{15-2(7)}
\\\\
&=1
\end{align}$

Now we can find the slope:

$\begin{align}
\dfrac{h(7)-h(3)}{7-3}&=\dfrac{1-3}{4}
\\\\
&=-\dfrac{1}{2}
\end{align}$
